we announced the podcast,

00:04:14.976 --> 00:04:16.350
at the same time
there was a blog

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.589
put out explaining that we have
a significantly expanded set

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:22.495
of products that Cloud audit
logging is now integrated with,

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.370
which is really cool.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.890
So its now works with Compute
Engine, Container Engine,

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:29.430
Dataproc, Deployment Manager,
Cloud DNS, Key Management

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.870
Service, Cloud
Storage, and Cloud SQL.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.300
The above integrations
are all in beta,

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.160
but it does work
across the board.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.020
So its pretty sweet.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.570
And the article
goes through how you

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.940
can interact with the audit
logs in cloud console,

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:45.060
how you can interact with
them and Stackdriver,

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.534
you can do alerts-- and
it even talks about,

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.950
if you're signed up for the
alpha for Cloud Functions, how

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.500
you can also use cloud functions
to interact with your audit

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.320
trails, as well.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.447
So you can have automatic
responses to certain actions

00:04:56.447 --> 00:04:58.530
that people take within
your Google Cloud Platform

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.450
project, which I think
is pretty cool as well.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:01.366
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:05:01.366 --> 00:05:04.680
So yeah, I think that
is important to remind

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.390
our listeners, just in case
you were wondering what

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:11.860
is the difference between Cloud
Audit logging and Google Cloud

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:12.580
IAM.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.705
Because sometimes it may
be a little bit confusing.

00:05:14.705 --> 00:05:16.220
The way I like to put it is--

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:20.590
Cloud IAM says who's
allowed to do what,

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:25.570
and Cloud Audit logging
says who did what.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.160
So it's not if you're
allowed or not.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.640
It's like, did you
actually do it?

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.860
So it's good for logging.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.539
Like if you have
something that people

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:35.080
are allowed to do but you want
to make sure they didn't do it

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.570
too often, or that they have
a reason behind it to do it,

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.237
that is the product to use.

00:05:40.237 --> 00:05:41.070
MARK MANDEL: Mm-hmm.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.120
Sounds good.

