00:29:35.910 --> 00:29:38.400
is we do have this thing
called a Cloud Storage Transfer

00:29:38.400 --> 00:29:41.760
Service, which is specifically
set up for transferring data

00:29:41.760 --> 00:29:44.550
from one cloud storage
provider to another,

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:46.380
which is kind of cool.

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:49.270
Obviously, you're going
to have network costs

00:29:49.270 --> 00:29:51.990
for moving from one to the
other, so keep that in mind.

00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:56.040
But you're able to set it up so
that you have basically sources

00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:56.550
and sinks.

00:29:56.550 --> 00:29:58.320
So like, where do you
want it to go from?

00:29:58.320 --> 00:30:00.144
Where do you want it to go to?

00:30:00.144 --> 00:30:01.560
And then you can
kind of set it up

00:30:01.560 --> 00:30:05.250
to happen like periodically,
or maybe just once off.

00:30:05.250 --> 00:30:08.820
There's a programmatic
interface.

00:30:08.820 --> 00:30:11.010
You can go through
the console UI,

00:30:11.010 --> 00:30:12.770
and there's a series
of REST APIs as well.

00:30:12.770 --> 00:30:14.478
So you can really kind
of pick and choose

00:30:14.478 --> 00:30:15.840
how you want it to work.

00:30:15.840 --> 00:30:18.421
But it is a nice and easy way
of just transferring that data

00:30:18.421 --> 00:30:20.670
across, if you need to do
that between different cloud

00:30:20.670 --> 00:30:21.594
providers.

00:30:21.594 --> 00:30:22.510
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:30:22.510 --> 00:30:25.210
That sounds,
indeed, very useful.

00:30:25.210 --> 00:30:27.010
I don't know how often
those kind of thing

00:30:27.010 --> 00:30:28.900
are needed to be
done, but if you're

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:31.680
thinking about starting to
try Google Cloud Platform,

00:30:31.680 --> 00:30:34.370
and it's like you need to
pass all your data around,

00:30:34.370 --> 00:30:35.871
it's probably the
best way to do it.

00:30:35.871 --> 00:30:36.620
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:30:36.620 --> 00:30:38.140
And I think it's kind of cool.

00:30:38.140 --> 00:30:39.940
It's one of those things that
you really need it when you

00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:41.856
need, but if you don't
need it then you don't.

00:30:41.856 --> 00:30:42.984
It's one or the other.

00:30:42.984 --> 00:30:43.900
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.130
MARK MANDEL: But if
you don't know it

00:30:45.130 --> 00:30:47.770
exists, then it could be really
painful to pull everything

00:30:47.770 --> 00:30:49.000
down, say, locally--

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.800
like via GSUtil--
and then push it

00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:52.409
back up again into the cloud.

00:30:52.409 --> 00:30:54.700
Whereas you'd much rather
run it over the big fat pipes

00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:56.950
that usually run between
all the big datacenters.

00:30:56.950 --> 00:30:58.991
FRANCESC CAMPOY: And if
you need to do syncing in

00:30:58.991 --> 00:31:02.230
between AWS and GCP,
I think that there

00:31:02.230 --> 00:31:04.130
is a thing that I
should mention--

00:31:04.130 --> 00:31:07.150
because it's tool written
in Go, and it's open source.

00:31:07.150 --> 00:31:08.560
It's called Mineo.

00:31:08.560 --> 00:31:11.800
And they're really cool,
because they're written in Go.

00:31:11.800 --> 00:31:13.870
So of course, it's a cool tool.

00:31:13.870 --> 00:31:14.920
But check it out.

00:31:14.920 --> 00:31:18.730
It actually supports a bunch
of different assorted services

00:31:18.730 --> 00:31:19.850
from different clouds.

00:31:19.850 --> 00:31:20.350
So there's--

00:31:20.350 --> 00:31:20.940
MARK MANDEL: Interesting.

00:31:20.940 --> 00:31:22.900
FRANCESC CAMPOY: --S3, but also
there's Google Cloud Storage.

00:31:22.900 --> 00:31:24.740
They have their
own Mineo server.

00:31:24.740 --> 00:31:26.980
It also supports
OpenStack Swift.

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:30.970
So it's definitely worth
having a look if what you need

00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:33.760
is a little bit more complex
than just passing from one side

00:31:33.760 --> 00:31:35.140
to the other ones.

00:31:35.140 --> 00:31:36.220
